{{ name }} at {{ ip }} — poll its API on an interval

SIEMBOX doesn't ship a generic API poller yet, so wire this up with cron on any
host that can reach {{ ip }} (the SIEMBOX host itself works) and forward each
response as syslog with `logger`:

*/5 * * * * curl -s -k -H "Authorization: Bearer $YOUR_TOKEN" \
  "https://{{ ip }}:{{ port }}{{ api_endpoint }}" \
  | logger -n {{ siembox_host }} -P {{ siembox_port }} -d -t {{ id }}

Replace $YOUR_TOKEN with the credential from the optional credential step
(see this source's fingerprint for what it unlocks). Adjust the */5 interval
to match how often {{ name }} rotates through new events, and swap https for
http if {{ name }} doesn't serve TLS on {{ port }}.
